@1F64 FDC_RESTORE_DRV
  Forgets the track of the drives in A (DISK_IO operation 0), selects them on the latch and
  restores the head (FDC_RESTORE).
  Entry: A = the drive bits; C = the controller's port base; H bits 0-1 = the step rate.
  Exit: A = 2 (NZ) when the head is at track 0, else 0.
  Changes: AF, B, E; IY-$17 to IY-$13 (the nested DISK_IO call), IY-$16, IY-$5F.
  Keeps: C, D, HL, IX, IY.
  .1F64 B = the drives
  .1F65 Operation 0
  .1F66 Forgets their tracks
  .1F69 The drive latch
  .1F6B Selects the drives
  .1F6D The command register

@1F71 FDC_TYPE1_CMD
  Issues a head command (restore, seek, step) with the step rate from H, waits for the head to load
  when the drive changed and for the motor to spin up when it was off (index pulses on latch bit
  0, bounded), then waits while the controller is busy.
  Entry: B = the command; C = the controller's port base; H bits 0-1 = the step rate; IY-$16 = the
  flags, IY-$17 = the operation.
  Exit: A = 2 (NZ) when the head is at track 0, else 0; IY-$16 = the flags, motor bit 7 set.
  Changes: AF, B, E; IY-$16, IY-$5F.
  Keeps: C, D, HL, IX, IY.
  .1F71 Keeps HL
  .1F72 The step rate
  .1F75 Issues the command
  .1F78 E = the flags
  .1F7B A = the operation
  .1F7E Operations 1 and 3 become 1
  .1F80 Read or verify?
  .1F81 Yes: no waits
  .1F83 A new drive?
  .1F87 Clears the mark
  .1F89 Waits for the head to load

question 1C9F What does the count at IY-$5F ($6E per command, $0A after operation 0 with B = 0) count down?
question 1CB1 Which segments give a port base other than $10 (half the segment, with bit 1 clear)?
question 1D40 Operation 8 with no drive returns A = 2 when drive 0 is not at track 0: is that a result its callers test?
question 1AB9 What does HL hold on entry to functions 8-11, which $12F9, $0EC3 and $1268 read?
question 1B01 What sets bit 1 of IY-$37 and the drive and cluster at IY+$60-$62 that delete refuses?
feedback missing 1C9F The card gives no port numbers: C comes from IN C,(C) on port $B3, so every IN/OUT (C) in the driver had to be traced by hand
feedback pattern 1C9F-1F89 The driver's IY-relative variables (IY-$1F to IY-$13) recur on 30 cards with no shared summary
feedback missing 1A37 The card says BC, HL change but the code restores both (POP BC at $1A6B, EX (SP),IX / POP HL at $1A92)
feedback wrong 1AA2 The facts say IY may change, but no path writes it: the only IY writes on the page are $0017, $0480 (restored at $04AC), $09B2 and DISK_IO's own (restored)
feedback wrong 1A37 BC and HL come back: POP BC at $1A6B and POP HL at $1A94 (the Keeps: warnings are settled from the code)
feedback listing 1148-11D8 Opened to learn what $1148, $1172, $1190 and $1193 take and return: callee contracts are not on the cards
